    "value": "Validates finite lmbench syscall, context-switch, memory-latency, memory-bandwidth, and pipe-bandwidth results"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Tools Executed",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run lmbench lat_syscall (null, read), lat_ctx, lat_mem_rd 16 128, bw_mem 512m rd, and bw_pipe"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Smoke Run (One minute or less)",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --smoke --validate --warmup-duration-us 1000 --repetitions 1"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Baseline Run (3 to 5 minutes)",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --baseline --validate --warmup-duration-us 10000 --repetitions 1"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Extended Run (8 to 15 minutes)",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --extended --validate --warmup-duration-us 10000 --repetitions 4"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Execution Details and Purpose",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run lmbench lat_syscall (null and read), lat_ctx, lat_mem_rd 16 128, bw_mem 512m rd, and bw_pipe once per yaml repetitions, then parse the first float, to measure syscall, context-switch, and memory-read latency plus memory and pipe bandwidth"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Run lmbench lat_syscall for null and read only, lat_ctx, lat_mem_rd 16 128, bw_mem 512m rd, and bw_pipe once per yaml repetitions, then parse the first float"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Runs a fixed lmbench subset from PATH or /usr/lib/lmbench/bin: lat_syscall (null and read only), lat_ctx, lat_mem_rd 16 128, bw_mem 512m rd, and bw_pipe. repetitions: suite repeats. warmup_duration_us: lmbench -W, microseconds each test runs untimed before it is timed (lat_mem_rd warms up once per array size). Every tool runs single-threaded (no -P)"
  },
